      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/d19c7802a136d6fd039c190acdda94e9e8603d58d2ba62864ea0e5522cbd6791.png)\n\nGiven the diagram above, where $|a|=3$ and $|b|=4$, find the value of $|a+b|.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the triangle law for adding the vectors $a$ and $b.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/3858242481fec9cd3b3fef85fcbb4e6a17aff20128f47565807a253dba517585.png)\n\nUsing the law of cosines, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2}-2|a||b|\\operatorname{cos}⁡({120}^{∘}) \\\\  & ={3}^{2}+{4}^{2}-2\\cdot 3\\cdot 4\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =9+16+12 \\\\  & =37\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|a+b|=\\sqrt{37}.$",
